       <span class=\"topic-title\">Connected To</span>\n            <span class=\"topic-count\">2</span>\n        </summary>\n\n        \n        <div class=\"topic-examples\">\n            \n                <a\n                    href=\"/james-bond/mi6/bond-007\"\n                    class=\"connection\"\n                    data-relationship=\"Connected To\"\n                >\n                    <strong>James Bond (007)</strong>\n                    <span>MI6 double-O agent with a licence to kill.</span>\n                </a>\n            \n                <a\n                    href=\"/james-bond/bond-theme\"\n                    class=\"connection\"\n                    data-relationship=\"Connected To\"\n                >\n                    <strong>James Bond Theme</strong>\n                    <span>The James Bond Theme is the main signature theme of the James Bond film series and is featured in every EON Productions 007 film since Dr. No in different versions. The piece has been used as the accompanying fanfare to…</span>\n                </a>\n            \n        </div>\n        \n\n        <div class=\"topic-content\">\n            \n                <div class=\"fact-card\">\n                    <div class=\"fact-label\">\n                        Connected To\n                    </div>\n\n                    <h3>\n        <a href=\"/james-bond/mi6/bond-007\" class=\"entity-link\">\n            James Bond (007)\n        </a>\n    </h3>\n\n                    <p>007 is the central figure of James Bond.</p>\n\n                    \n\n                    \n                </div>\n            \n                <div class=\"fact-card\">\n                    <div class=\"fact-label\">\n                        Connected To\n                    </div>\n\n                    <h3>\n        <a href=\"/james-bond/bond-theme\" class=\"entity-link\">\n            James Bond Theme\n        </a>\n    </h3>\n\n                    <p>The Bond Theme identifies the franchise.</p>\n\n                    \n\n                    \n                </div>\n            \n        </div>\n    </details>\n</section>\n\n<section class=\"topic-section\">\n    <details>\n        <summary class=\"topic-summary\">\n            <span class=\"topic-title\">Created By</span>\n            <span class=\"topic-count\">1</span>\n        </summary>\n\n        \n\n        <div class=\"topic-content\">\n            \n                <div class=\"fact-card\">\n                    <div class=\"fact-label\">\n                        Created By\n                    </div>\n\n                    <h3>\n        <a href=\"/james-bond/ian-fleming\" class=\"entity-link\">\n            Ian Fleming\n        </a>\n    </h3>\n\n                    <p>Ian Fleming created James Bond.</p>\n\n                    \n\n                    \n                </div>\n            \n        </div>\n    </details>\n</section>\n\n<section class=\"topic-section\">\n    <details>\n        <summary class=\"topic-summary\">\n            <span class=\"topic-title\">Produced By</span>\n            <span class=\"topic-count\">1</span>\n        </summary>\n\n        \n\n        <div class=\"topic-content\">\n            \n                <div class=\"fact-card\">\n                    <div class=\"fact-label\">\n                        Produced By\n                    </div>\n\n                    <h3>\n        <a href=\"/james-bond/eon-productions\" class=\"entity-link\">\n            Eon Productions\n        </a>\n    </h3>\n\n                    <p>Eon Productions produces the Bond films.</p>\n\n                    \n\n                    \n                </div>\n            \n        </div>\n    </details>\n</section>\n\n</section>\n\n\n<section class=\"did-you-know\">\n    <h2>Did you know?</h2>\n    <ul>\n        <li>James Bond is also referenced as 007 franchise, Bond, Bond series.</li><li>007 is the central figure of James Bond.</li><li>Ian Fleming created James Bond.</li><li>Eon Productions produces the Bond films.</li><li>Dr. No begins the Eon film series.</li><li>Evidence around James Bond is classified as fiction on Ton-o-Lore.</li>\n    </ul>\n</section>","overview":"<section class=\"overview\">\n    <h2>What is James Bond?</h2>\n    \n    <p>\n        The James Bond franchise focuses on the character of James Bond, a fictional British Secret Service agent created in 1953 by writer <a href=\"/james-bond/ian-fleming\" class=\"entity-link\">Ian Fleming</a>, who featured him in twelve novels and two short-story collections. Since Fleming&#039;s death in 1964, nine other authors have written authorised Bond novels or novelisations: Kingsley Amis, Christopher Wood, John Gardner, Raymond Benson, Sebastian Faulks, Jeffery Deaver, William Boyd, Anthony Horowitz and Charlie Higson. The latest novel is On His Majesty&#039;s Secret Service by Charlie Higson, published in May 2023. Charlie Higson wrote a series on a young James Bond, and Kate Westbrook wrote three novels based on the diaries of a recurring series character, Moneypenny.\n    </p>\n    <p>\n        The character—also known by the code number <a href=\"/james-bond/007-forever-and-a-day\" class=\"entity-link\">007</a> (pronounced &quot;double-oh-seven&quot;)—has also been adapted for television, radio, comic strips, video games and film. The James Bond franchise is one of the highest-grossing media franchises of all time. The films constitute one of the longest continually running film series and have grossed over US$7.04 billion in total at the box office, making James Bond the fifth-highest-grossing film series to date. It started in 1962 with <a href=\"/james-bond/dr-no\" class=\"entity-link\">Dr. No</a>, starring Sean Connery as Bond. As of 2021, there have been twenty-five films in the <a href=\"/james-bond/eon-productions\" class=\"entity-link\">Eon Productions</a> series. The most recent Bond film, <a href=\"/james-bond/no-time-to-die\" class=\"entity-link\">No Time to Die</a> (2021), stars Daniel Craig in his fifth and final portrayal of Bond; he is the sixth actor to play Bond in the Eon series. There have also been two independent Bond film productions: <a href=\"/james-bond/casino-royale\" class=\"entity-link\">Casino Royale</a> (a 1967 spoof starring David Niven) and Never Say Never Again (a 1983 remake of an earlier Eon-produced film, 1965&#039;s <a href=\"/james-bond/thunderball\" class=\"entity-link\">Thunderball</a>, both starring Connery). <a href=\"/james-bond/casino-royale\" class=\"entity-link\">Casino Royale</a> has also been adapted for television, as a one-hour show in 1954 as part of the CBS series Climax!.\n    </p>\n    <p>\n        The Bond films are renowned for a number of features, including their soundtracks; three of the movies&#039; theme songs have received Academy Awards and others have received nominations. Other important elements which run through most of the films include Bond&#039;s cars, his guns, and the gadgets with which he is supplied by Q Branch. The films are also noted for Bond&#039;s relationships with various women, who are popularly referred to as &quot;Bond girls&quot;.\n    </p>\n    \n    <p class=\"also-known-as\">\n        <strong>Also known as:</strong>\n        007 franchise, Bond, Bond series.\n    </p>\n\n</section>","word_count":1087,"uniqueness_score":"1.0000"},"entity":{"id":"4369b63d-baea-4f1b-ad85-e6d57227a8bd","name":"James Bond","slug":"james-bond","type":"topic","kind":"topic","type_label":"Topic","short_description":"The James Bond franchise focuses on the character of James Bond, a fictional British Secret Service agent created in 1953 by writer Ian Fleming, who featured him in twelve novels and two short-story collections. Since…","description":"The James Bond franchise focuses on the character of James Bond, a fictional British Secret Service agent created in 1953 by writer Ian Fleming, who featured him in twelve novels and two short-story collections. Since Fleming's death in 1964, nine other authors have written authorised Bond novels or novelisations: Kingsley Amis, Christopher Wood, John Gardner, Raymond Benson, Sebastian Faulks, Jeffery Deaver, William Boyd, Anthony Horowitz and Charlie Higson. The latest novel is On His Majesty's Secret Service by Charlie Higson, published in May 2023. Charlie Higson wrote a series on a young James Bond, and Kate Westbrook wrote three novels based on the diaries of a recurring series character, Moneypenny.\n\nThe character—also known by the code number 007 (pronounced \"double-oh-seven\")—has also been adapted for television, radio, comic strips, video games and film. The James Bond franchise is one of the highest-grossing media franchises of all time.  The films constitute one of the longest continually running film series and have grossed over US$7.04 billion in total at the box office, making James Bond the fifth-highest-grossing film series to date. It started in 1962 with Dr. No, starring Sean Connery as Bond. As of 2021, there have been twenty-five films in the Eon Productions series. The most recent Bond film, No Time to Die (2021), stars Daniel Craig in his fifth and final portrayal of Bond; he is the sixth actor to play Bond in the Eon series. There have also been two independent Bond film productions: Casino Royale (a 1967 spoof starring David Niven) and Never Say Never Again (a 1983 remake of an earlier Eon-produced film, 1965's Thunderball, both starring Connery). Casino Royale has also been adapted for television, as a one-hour show in 1954 as part of the CBS series Climax!.\n\nThe Bond films are renowned for a number of features, including their soundtracks; three of the movies' theme songs have received Academy Awards and others have received nominations. Other important elements which run through most of the films include Bond's cars, his guns, and the gadgets with which he is supplied by Q Branch. The films are also noted for Bond's relationships with various women, who are popularly referred to as \"Bond girls\".","evidence":"fiction","universe":"james-bond","aliases":["007 franchise","Bond","Bond series"],"wikipedia_url":null,"image_url":null,"image_source":null,"image_credit":null,"image_license":null,"image_usage":null,"image_alt":null},"connections":[{"id":"3676ac35-01c2-4050-a70e-5b1254ee94ea","relationship":"part_of","title":"Part of","explanation":"Part of","strength":"0.9000","discovery_score":"0.8500","direction":"incoming","from_entity_id":"9a688bf5-d9fe-47ca-8fdc-75ddc071a5e7","to_entity_id":"4369b63d-baea-4f1b-ad85-e6d57227a8bd","entity_id":"9a688bf5-d9fe-47ca-8fdc-75ddc071a5e7","slug":"belluna","name":"Belluna","type":"place","short_description":"Belluna was a fictional coastal village in California, United States; implied to lie along the coast of the Pacific Ocean. With a population of 27 employed primarily in fishing and agriculture, the tiny settlement…","evidence":"fiction","image_url":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/jamesbond/images/f/f2/Belluna%2C_California_%281%29.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/180?cb=20200402100125","path":"/james-bond/belluna","kind":"location","type_label":"Location"}],"rabbit_holes":[],"copyright":{"theme":"james-bond","title":"James Bond is not owned by Ton-o-Lore.","body":"James Bond, 007, and related names, characters, and imagery are the property of their respective rights holders, including Ian Fleming Publications Ltd., Danjaq LLC, Eon Productions, Metro-Goldwyn-Mayer, and other credited rights holders. Ton-o-Lore is an independent, unofficial fan and informational project and is not affiliated with or endorsed by those rights holders. Identification logos and thumbnails, when shown, are low-resolution images used under a fair-use rationale for commentary and identification only — not free or redistributable artwork."},"subject":{"id":"james-bond","name":"James Bond","theme":"james-bond","path":"/james-bond","logo":{"license":"fair_use","usage":"fair_use_identification","url":"htt